cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CarbonCreditBuy in research, teaching or a report, please cite
  it using the metadata below. Estimates produced with the software are
  scenario estimates, not certified carbon credits; please keep that
  distinction in any publication.
type: software
title: "CarbonCreditBuy: An Open, Explainable Platform for Estimating Tree-Based Carbon Removal and Its Indicative Credit Value on Farmland"
abstract: >-
  An open-source geospatial platform that helps farmers, landowners and
  researchers understand tree cover, agricultural conditions and potential
  carbon benefits, and what evidence they still need for a recognised
  carbon or environmental programme. It combines Earth-observation data
  (ESA WorldCover, Copernicus Sentinel-2), deterministic carbon models
  (IPCC 2006 Tier 1 gain-loss, Chave 2014 allometry) and configuration-driven
  regional policy screening for India, the United States and the European
  Union, with privacy-preserving handling of farm geometry.
